Third-party notices
===================

1. Kyutai REKI (https://github.com/kyutai-labs/reki, commit b2a3393), MIT License.

   This repository does not vendor REKI; scripts/setup.sh clones it into third_party/ (git-ignored).
   Parts of this repository are derived from REKI's code:
   - src/mk_expert.py and archive/mk_expert_v*.py re-implement the forward pass of REKI's action
     expert (RekiFlowModel._expert_step: AdaRMS modulation, gated residuals, self-attention over
     cached register K/V, cross-attention to the VLM, SiLU MLP, fp32 action projections, Euler
     update) as Triton kernels, and `install()` replaces RekiFlowModel._expert_actions with an
     adapted copy that keeps REKI's own _step_modulations / _expert_first_step calls.
   - src/fast_host.py contains a copy of RekiPolicy.predict (passing the camera arrays on instead of
     PIL images) and re-implements FastQwenImageProcessor's normalization and patchify on the GPU.
   - src/fast_prefill.py subclasses REKI's PrefillGraphs / _LayoutGraph and adapts
     PrefillGraphs.__call__.
   - src/harness.py, src/profile_breakdown.py and the other scripts call and instrument REKI's
     inference API (RekiPolicy, its CUDA-graph caches and register cache).
   These derived parts are covered by Kyutai's notice below in addition to this repository's LICENSE.

   The REKI model weights (kyutai/reki-2b-libero) are licensed CC-BY-NC-SA 4.0 and are not
   included; scripts/setup.sh downloads them from Hugging Face.

2. LIBERO frames (HuggingFaceVLA/libero on Hugging Face) are downloaded at run time, not included.

